---
import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';

const page = {
  path: '/saas-seo-services/',
  title: 'SaaS SEO Services for Software Companies | Bright Forge',
  description: 'SaaS SEO from our Philippines team: feature, comparison and integration pages, technical review and reporting tied to sign-ups. See our TeamStats case study.',
  h1: 'SaaS SEO Services for Software Companies',
  crumb: 'SaaS SEO',
  parents: [{ name: 'Industries', url: '/industries/' }],
  lead: [
    'People choosing software search for the problem, then for types of product, then for comparisons and integrations. We build and improve the pages for each stage and measure what reaches a trial or demo.',
  ],
  secondary: { href: '/case-studies/football-app-seo/', label: 'Read the TeamStats case study' },
  sections: [
    {
      h2: 'Software work you can check',
      html: `<ul class="bf-results">
<li><span class="bf-num">200,000 to 268,000</span><span class="bf-what"><strong>TeamStats</strong> (teamstats.net), a team management app for grassroots football: organic clicks over three months, compared with the same months a year earlier (rounded)</span><a class="bf-src" href="/case-studies/football-app-seo/">Case study</a></li>
<li><span class="bf-num">AI referral review</span><span class="bf-what"><strong>TeamStats:</strong> which pages AI tools sent visitors to, and what we recommended</span><a class="bf-src" href="/case-studies/ai-sports-saas-geo/">Review</a></li>
<li><span class="bf-num">AI referral review</span><span class="bf-what"><strong>A fintech software company</strong> (not named)</span><a class="bf-src" href="/case-studies/ai-fintech-saas-geo/">Review</a></li>
</ul>
<p>The figures are search clicks, not sign-ups.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'What we work on',
      html: `<dl class="bf-deliverables">
<dt>Feature and use-case pages</dt><dd>That say plainly what the product does and for whom.</dd>
<dt>Comparison and alternative pages</dt><dd>Written fairly and kept current.</dd>
<dt>Integration pages</dt><dd>One for each integration buyers search for.</dd>
<dt>Help and documentation</dt><dd>What should be indexed and what should not.</dd>
<dt>Technical review</dt><dd>Of JavaScript-heavy marketing sites and apps. See <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">technical SEO</a>.</dd>
<dt>AI search</dt><dd>How AI tools describe the product. See <a href="/ai-search-optimization-services-philippines/">AI search optimisation</a>.</dd>
<dt>Tracking</dt><dd>From search visit to sign-up.</dd>
</dl>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'How we do it',
      html: `<ol class="bf-steps">
<li>Map searches to the stages of the buying decision.</li>
<li>Audit the marketing site and the indexable parts of the app.</li>
<li>Write or rewrite the highest-value pages with your product team's input, through our <a href="/content-seo-services-philippines/">SEO content</a> process.</li>
<li>Report monthly on visits, sign-ups and the pages that produced them.</li>
</ol>
<p>For sports software, see also <a href="/football-soccer-seo-services/">football SEO</a>.</p>`,
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { question: 'Do you report sign-ups or only traffic?', answer: 'We agree which event can be measured reliably, such as a trial, a demo request or an install, and report that alongside search clicks. Search clicks are not labelled as pipeline or revenue when the connection has not been established.' },
  ],
};
---
<EditorialPage page={page} />
